  "narrative": "I reassessed the newly delivered discovery results using the same outcome-specific clinical-significance rules: for outcome_014 positive contrasts, I treated a 95% lower bound above about 0.0093 as sufficient; for outcome_001 claims registered with direction -1, I treated a 95% lower bound above about 0.0415 as sufficient. The joint robustness checks for the central feature_027 association were highly supportive. H55, the feature_027=1 versus 0 comparison within feature_034=1 and feature_002=1, gave +0.7928 [0.7520, 0.8336], and H56, the same comparison within feature_034=0 and feature_002=0, gave +0.8106 [0.7699, 0.8514]. Both lower bounds are far above the outcome_014 threshold, so these provide strong dataset-specific evidence that the very large positive feature_027 association persists in these joint binary-marker cells. The corresponding formal interaction tests were near null: H53 interaction with feature_034 was -0.0156 [-0.0561, 0.0248], H54 interaction with feature_002 was -0.0013 [-0.0417, 0.0391], and H75 interaction with feature_050 was -0.0089 [-0.0591, 0.0413]. None is accepted as clinically meaningful positive effect modification. Because several intervals still include small positive effects above the clinical threshold, I kept these as unresolved but closed them; they do not appear to be productive follow-up targets. The conditional feature_030 and feature_006 screens within feature_027=1 also do not support new associations. H115 was essentially null, +0.0012 [-0.0561, 0.0585], with a small comparator cell (n=43). H117 had a positive point estimate +0.0264 [-0.0357, 0.0885] above the clinical point threshold, but it was based on a very small exposed cell (n=22) and a wide interval, so it cannot be accepted from discovery data alone. Given multiplicity and the small cell, I left H117 unresolved and requested independent validation as the single most useful new validation. For outcome_001 within feature_050=1, H120, H121, and H122 showed small positive signed estimates +0.0147, +0.0159, and +0.0188 with intervals whose upper bounds only just exceed the outcome_001 clinical threshold; these do not support independent residual associations and were closed as unresolved. H124 and H125 had signed estimates opposing the registered negative raw direction, and their upper bounds were below the outcome_001 threshold, so they were rejected. Overall, these results strengthen the central dataset-specific associations, especially feature_027 with outcome_014 and feature_050 with outcome_001, while providing little support for additional independent predictors in the tested conditional cells. These remain associations within the supplied dataset and specified eligibility definitions, not causal or externally generalizable conclusions.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 12 appraise update. Joint checks confirm the dominant feature_027 association with outcome_014 across feature_034/feature_002 combinations: H55 and H56 accepted. Formal effect-modification tests by feature_034, feature_002, and feature_050 on the feature_027 association are near null and closed unresolved. Conditional screening within feature_050=1 for outcome_001 mostly showed no meaningful residual associations; H124 and H125 rejected, H120-H122 closed unresolved. Within feature_027=1 for outcome_014, feature_030 appears null; feature_006/H117 is the only borderline candidate with a point estimate above threshold but an extremely small exposed cell (n=22). H117 validation is requested before further pursuit. Do not revisit feature_054 heterogeneity unless independent evidence strongly reopens it. Future allocations should prioritize validation results for H117 and any broad screening that can identify another predictor with convergent, well-powered evidence, rather than small-cell or marginal screening contrasts."
